import json,re
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
p=root/'research.md'; text=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
text=text.replace('qualify matching with small Entur Journey Planner lookups first','first test matching with small Entur Journey Planner lookups')
text=text.replace('National Stop Registry references','National Stop Registry (NSR) references')
text=text.replace('NLOD reuse requires','Reuse under the Norwegian Licence for Open Government Data (NLOD) requires')
text=text.replace('DST is more subtle','Daylight saving time (DST) is more subtle')
text=text.replace('The invalid service date2026-10-26 produced zero calls.','The query for 2026-10-26, when this service did not operate, returned zero calls.')
text=text.replace('independently published Svipper timetable','separately published Svipper timetable')
text=text.replace('**Independent control:**','**Local publication cross-check:**')
text=text.replace('**Cross-checked:** different underlying sources agree on the stated narrow claim. High confidence within that boundary.','**Cross-checked:** separately published sources agree on a narrow claim. High confidence requires independent underlying evidence; agreement between Svipper and Entur alone does not establish independent data lineage.')
text=text.replace('Medium observed; high only for independently checked sample','Medium observed; upstream independence unverified')
text=text.replace('one independent timetable match','one cross-publication timetable match')
text=text.replace('The principal unresolved issue','Svipper and Entur may share upstream planning data; their agreement is a useful publication check, not independently generated ground truth.\n\nThe principal unresolved issue')
# Preserve exact identifiers, URLs and literal code while fixing joined prose/value boundaries.
parts=re.split(r'(`[^`]*`|https?://[^\s)]+)',text)
for i,s in enumerate(parts):
 if i%2: continue
 s=re.sub(r'(?<=[A-Za-zÆØÅæøå])(?=\d)', ' ', s)
 s=re.sub(r'(?<=\d)(h)\b',r' \1',s)
 s=re.sub(r',(?=\d{4}\b)',', ',s)
 s=re.sub(r';(?=\S)','; ',s)
 s=re.sub(r'(?<=[.!?:])(?=\[\d+\])',' ',s)
 s=s.replace('→',' → ')
 parts[i]=s
text=''.join(parts).replace('V 1','V1').replace('an separately published','a separately published')
# Put the coverage definition before the option comparison.
start=text.index('### A measurable definition of complete')
end=text.index('\n## 2.',start)
block=text[start:end].strip()
text=text[:start]+text[end:]
anchor='## 1. Access choices and completeness\n'
text=text.replace(anchor,anchor+'\n'+block+'\n\n### Access comparison\n',1)
# Replace placeholder with generated staleness rows (numeric source markers stay citations, not appendix keys).
stale=json.loads((root/'checks/staleness.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
rows=['| Tracked claim | Class | Source/observation date | Computed recheck | State |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
for c in stale['claims']:
 ref=re.match(r'\[(\d+)\]',c['claim']).group(1)
 rows.append(f"| Claim [{ref}] | {c['class']} | {c['pub_date']} | {c['recheck']} | {'Due' if c['stale'] else 'Within window'} |")
ending='\n'.join(rows)+'\n\nComputed with the installed `recon_kit.py staleness` helper: landscape 12 months, patterns 24 months, versions/compatibility 1 month, and live observations 1 month (a conservative run-specific freshness cap). Source publication dates are preserved; observed data uses its actual observation date. Earliest computed recheck is **'+stale['earliest_recheck']+'**, already due for the realtime compatibility claim. Its current page was reread during this run, but independent feed qualification is still missing; recheck it before implementing the notice adapter. Live observations next reach the one-month cap on **2026-11-26**, and should be refreshed sooner when planning data changes. This table is a refresh work order, not a source availability guarantee.\n\n## Validation and delivery boundary\n\nMechanical citation check resolves all 24 source markers with no missing or orphaned rows. Fresh-context semantic checking found no load-bearing mismatch and identified the shared-upstream confidence caveat, now reflected above. Structure/prose findings were applied; exact observations and identifiers were preserved. Source digests and checks document remaining extraction limits. No red-team pass or product test was run.\n\nThe ledger counts are generated by the installed helper: **2 independently verified conceptual claims and 10 unverified claims**, where unverified includes single-publisher documented/observed facts and does not mean falsified. Cross-publication agreement for the Svipper sample is retained without claiming independent underlying data. Research is complete within these bounds; the open qualification gates remain open. No implementation, V1 edits, database/service actions, merge, push or commit occurred.\n'
text=text.replace('Machine-generated refresh dates and final claim counts are appended after ledger verification. Source observations and mutable assets must be rechecked before implementation; profile documentation age is preserved rather than replaced by its access date.',ending)
text=text.replace('status: draft','status: complete',1).replace('validation: normal','validation: normal\nclaims_verified: 2\nclaims_unverified: 10',1)
p.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
print('Applied editorial and semantic corrections; added generated staleness map and final metadata.')

